%I A400914 #7 Oct 14 2026 23:19:05
%S A400914 1,1,9,78,1693,162465
%N A400914 Number of nonisomorphic g-dimonoids of order n.
%C A400914 A g-dimonoid is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms:
%C A400914    (x -| y) -| z = x -| (y |- z),
%C A400914    (x -| y) |- z = x |- (y |- z).
%H A400914 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.30970/ms.66.1.24-37">On the number of g-dimonoids of small order</a>, Mat. Stud. 66(1) (2026), 24-37.
%H A400914 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.29641">On the number of g-dimonoids of small order</a>, arXiv:2607.29641 [math.GR] (2026).
%H A400914 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22646257">Lists of all pairwise nonisomorphic g-dimonoids of orders up to 5</a>, Zenodo (2026).
%H A400914 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://gist.github.com/vgavrylkiv/32700f9f64e7e7d81a79f676716b3e64">Python code for computing nonisomorphic g-dimonoids</a>, GitHub Gist (2026).
%e A400914 For n = 2, there are exactly 9 pairwise nonisomorphic g-dimonoids (D,-|,|-) on the set D={0,1}. Rows and columns are ordered as 0,1. The Cayley tables of all nine g-dimonoids are listed below.
%e A400914 g-dimonoid #1:
%e A400914    -|:   |-:
%e A400914    0 0   0 0
%e A400914    0 0   0 0
%e A400914 g-dimonoid #2:
%e A400914    -|:   |-:
%e A400914    0 0   0 1
%e A400914    0 0   0 1
%e A400914 g-dimonoid #3:
%e A400914    -|:   |-:
%e A400914    0 1   0 1
%e A400914    1 0   1 0
%e A400914 g-dimonoid #4:
%e A400914    -|:   |-:
%e A400914    0 0   0 0
%e A400914    0 1   0 1
%e A400914 g-dimonoid #5:
%e A400914    -|:   |-:
%e A400914    0 0   0 0
%e A400914    1 1   0 0
%e A400914 g-dimonoid #6:
%e A400914    -|:   |-:
%e A400914    0 0   0 0
%e A400914    1 1   1 1
%e A400914 g-dimonoid #7:
%e A400914    -|:   |-:
%e A400914    0 0   0 1
%e A400914    1 1   0 1
%e A400914 g-dimonoid #8:
%e A400914    -|:   |-:
%e A400914    0 1   0 1
%e A400914    0 1   0 1
%e A400914 g-dimonoid #9:
%e A400914    -|:   |-:
%e A400914    0 0   1 1
%e A400914    0 0   1 1
